CleanFinder 1.0 — User Manual

Genotyping Analysis Tool v1.0.0

Developed by Andrea Rossi — IUF Leibniz Research Institute,EACR Lab & GEMD Core Unit, Düsseldorf


1. Introduction

What Is CleanFinder?

CleanFinder is a genotyping analysis platform engineered to categorize NGS sequencing reads with high precision. By utilizing a constrained glocal alignment algorithm, it compares amplicon reads against a reference sequence to accurately identify a comprehensive range of genomic modifications, including:

Standard Indels: Wildtype, deletions, and insertions.

Targeted Substitutions: Base editing and knock-ins.

Complex Rearrangements: Large-scale Prime Editing and custom multi-variant outcomes.

CleanFinder is available in two forms:

CleanFinder is designed to be flexible, offering a client-side Web App for instant, visual analysis and a Python CLI for high-throughput bioinformatics pipelines.


Feature	Web App (Browser-Native)	Python CLI
Primary Platform	Any OS via Web Browser	Command-line (Python 3.7+)
Best For	Interactive exploration & visual QC	Batch processing & automated pipelines
Operational Modes	Standard: Full alignment detail
Turbo: Rapid heuristic processing	Single: Individual FASTQ analysis
Batch: Parallel multi-sample processing
Data Privacy	Local execution: Data never leaves your machine	Local execution: Fully offline environment
Core Outputs	Interactive dashboards, heatmaps, & CSVs	Console summaries & structured CSV exports


Supported Sequencing Data

- Illumina — Short-read amplicon sequencing (paired-end or single-end)
- Oxford Nanopore (ONT) — Short- and Long- Long-read amplicon data
- PacBio — Short- and Long-read amplicon data

Input format: FASTQ files (`.fastq`, `.fq`). The Python CLI also accepts FASTA reference files.

