2. Web App — Standard Mode

The Standard Mode web app (`www.CleanFinder.org`) provides a full-featured dashboard with a sidebar for configuration and a main panel for results.

2.1 Interface Overview

The interface is divided into:

- Sidebar (left) 
— Configuration: reference sequence, gRNA, analysis mode, parameters, and file upload
- Main Panel (right;
 — Results: File overview (Grid vs Heatmap), Edit Distribution (Categories vs Indel types, Card (Total reads, Editing Efficiency, Out-of-frame %, In-of-frame %, Precise % (KI, BE, PE), Genotype Distribution,  min. read cut-off, min. %, min. Phred, Allel type (e.g. del.), delta (e.g. -13), frame (e.g. out-of-frame), aligned sequence, REPEIRome (e.g. MMHJ, MH: 3bp, PAM distal (10bp), number of reads, and %.  
Additional charts: Indel size, frame distribution, microhomology length distribution, Repair Pathway (RIMA), PAM proximity deletion.
Clone summary: File Name, Total Reads, Efficiency Knock-in %,	In-Frame %, Out-of-Frame %,	MMEJ % (of Deletions) exportable in .csv. 

2.2 Setting Up a Reference

Paste Reference Sequence

1. Open the app in your browser
2. In the sidebar, paste your wildtype amplicon sequence into the "Reference Sequence" field
3. Paste your gRNA sequence into the gRNA Sequence field (Required for Anchors). If not the app will analyze your data in blind mode (w/o centering around the gRNA).
3. The app will automatically detect anchors (the flanking regions used to extract the editing window from each read)

Fetch from Gene Symbol

Alternatively, you can fetch a reference directly from Ensembl/UCSC:

1. Enter a Gene Symbol (e.g., `VHL`, `TP53`)
2. Optionally enter a gRNA sequence — this ensures the reference is centered on your target site
3. Click Fetch — the app retrieves X bp (the size of the bp can be set in the padding field below) centered on the gRNA cut site

gRNA Sequence

Enter your guide RNA (gRNA) sequence (without PAM). This is used to:
- Center the analysis window on the cut site
- Highlight the gRNA position in alignment views
- Mark the PAM site in the reference

2.3 Analysis Modes

Select the appropriate mode from the sidebar dropdown:

CleanFinder uses specialized alignment parameters tailored to the unique "molecular signatures" of different CRISPR systems. Selecting the correct mode ensures the highest possible accuracy for variant calling.


Mode	Primary Use Case	Algorithmic Logic
Cas9	Standard Indel detection	Optimized for small indels centered around the 3bp upstream of the PAM site.
Cas12	Cpf1 / Cas12a editing	Adjusted for distal 5' staggered cuts, allowing for a larger search window for characteristic deletions.
Prime Editing	Precise PE insertions/swaps	Uses relaxed gap penalties to prioritize the "Edit" sequence (pegRNA template) over the wildtype sequence.
Base Editing	CBE / ABE transitions	Employs heavy gap penalties to suppress indel calls, focusing exclusively on high-confidence nucleotide substitutions (C → T or A → G).


Mode-Specific Parameters

- HDR Template (optional) — Expected knock-in sequence. Reads matching this are classified as "KI".
- PE Edit Sequence (Prime Editing mode) — The expected edited sequence.
- BE Conversion (Base Editing mode) — The expected base conversion pattern (e.g., `C → T`).

2.4 Advanced Parameters

Located under "Advanced Settings" in the sidebar:


Parameter	Default	Purpose
Anchor Length	20 bp	The "stable" sequence length flanking your target site used to lock the alignment in place.
Max Mismatches	2	Number of allowed errors in the anchor regions (enables "fuzzy matching" for low-quality or polymorphic samples).
Min Phred Score	0	The quality threshold; reads with an average score below this are discarded to prevent "false" variant calls.


In Advanced Alignment Parameters, you gain manual control over the alignment scoring matrix. This is critical for non-standard nucleases or highly repetitive regions.


Setting	Function
Match	Reward score for identical bases.
Mismatch	Penalty score for base differences (higher values = stricter substitution calling).
Gap Open	Penalty for initiating a deletion or insertion (higher values = fewer indels).
Gap Ext.	Penalty for extending an existing gap (higher values = shorter indels).

2.5 Uploading Reads

FASTQ Files
- Click "Upload FASTQ" in the sidebar
- Select one or more `.fastq` / `.fq` files

Paste Sequences (only in Turbo mode)
- Alternatively, paste raw sequences directly (one per line) or paste FASTQ-formatted text

2.6 Running Analysis

1. Click "Start Analysis" 
2. Live Progress Tracking: The interface transitions to a real-time monitor. You don’t have to wonder if the app has frozen; CleanFinder provides live telemetry:
-	Throughput: Displays the number of reads being processed per second. 
-	ETA: A dynamic countdown showing exactly when your results will be ready.
-	Progress Bar: A visual representation of the total FASTQ file completion.
3. Results appear in the main panel

2.7 Understanding Results

Summary Badges
At the top of results, badges show key metrics:
- Total Reads — Number of input reads
- Edited % — Proportion of edited reads

Allele Table
Each unique genotype is listed as a row showing:
- Call — Rank by frequency (wt always on top if available)
- Type — WT, DEL, INS, SNP, KI, PE, BE
- Δ (Delta) — Size difference from reference (e.g., -3 = 3bp deletion)
- Frame — In-Frame or Out-of-Frame
- Reads — Count and percentage
- Alignment — Visual alignment against reference with highlighted mutations
- REPAIRome (MMEJ, NHEJ, ME size, PAM distance)

Alignment View
For each allele, the alignment shows:
- Reference row — The wildtype sequence
- Read row — The mutant sequence
- Highlighted regions — gRNA in yellow, PAM in red, mutations in color
- Deletions appear as dashes (`-`), insertions as extra bases

Summary Charts
- Pie chart — Distribution of editing outcomes (WT, In-Frame, Out-of-Frame, SNP, HDR)
- Indel Size Distribution — Bar chart showing the frequency of each indel size
- Additional Charts (Indels, Frameshifts, RIMA
- Clones Summary (all stats)

- Color legend (shown above the plate):
  - 🟢 Green — KI/PE
  - 🟣 Purple — BE
  - 🔵 Blue — WT
  - 🔴 Red — Deletion ( 🔴 Out-of-Frame Indel, 🔵In-Frame Indel)
  - 🟡 Amber - SNP

